Memory barriers in .NET
Threading models work differently on single-core versus multicore processors. On single-
core processors, only one thread gets a CPU slice while other threads wait for their turn.
This ensures that whenever a thread accesses the memory (for loading and storing), it is in
the right order. This model is also known as a sequential consistency model. In the case of
multicore processor systems, multiple threads run concurrently. Sequential consistency is
not guaranteed in these systems since either the hardware or the Just in Time (JIT)

