ExecuteNonQuery is another method that is mainly used to execute non-query methods,
such as INSERT, UPDATE, and DELETE. When you insert some data into a database, you are
not querying anything in the database, you just want to insert the data. The same goes for
update and delete. The ExecuteNonQuery method returns an INT value, which represents
how many rows in the database were affected by the command. For example, if you are
inserting a person in a Person table, you are inserting one new row in the table, so only
one row is getting affected. The method will therefore return 1 to you.
Let's see an example code of the ExecuteNonQuery() method:
